summary_en.experiments:
Uses three recent agent benchmarks as the “real” datasets: T1, BFCL, and ACP. Synthetic datasets are generated with NVIDIA NeMo and custom generators designed to emulate common pitfalls (e.g., degraded fidelity, low diversity). Results indicate:
- SynAE metrics capture fine-grained variations across validity/fidelity/diversity;
- no single metric is sufficient;
- downstream-consistency checks can reveal synthetic biases that would otherwise mislead evaluation.
(The provided excerpt does not include full quantitative tables, so exact numeric deltas per benchmark cannot be reliably quoted here.)
